@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 30px auto; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333;">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last Updated: @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM yyyy")</strong></p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>NZFTC EMS (Employee Management System) is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, store, and protect personal information through our employee management system.</p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect the following categories of personal information:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Employee Data:</strong> Name, email, contact information, address, date of birth, employee ID, job role, department assignment, employment status, and employment dates</li>
        <li><strong>Payroll Information:</strong> Salary, tax file number details, banking information, deductions, leave balances, and payment history</li>
        <li><strong>Grievance Records:</strong> Formal complaints, investigation notes, resolution details, and related correspondence</li>
        <li><strong>Access Logs:</strong> Login history, system activity, and timestamps of actions taken within the system</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>Your personal information is used for:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Employment management and payroll processing</li>
        <li>Compliance with employment legislation and tax requirements</li>
        <li>Leave and attendance tracking</li>
        <li>Grievance and dispute resolution</li>
        <li>System security and fraud prevention</li>
        <li>Performance and operational reporting</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We implement appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect your personal data against unauthorized access, alteration, or destruction. Access to the system is restricted based on your account type (Administrator or Standard User) and departmental role.</p>

    <h2>5. Access and User Roles</h2>
    <p>The system operates with two account types with different access levels:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Administrator:</strong> Full access to all employee data, payroll, and grievance records</li>
        <li><strong>Standard User:</strong> Access limited to their assigned department and role-specific menu paths</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Users can only access information relevant to their role and department responsibilities.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>Personal data is retained only as long as necessary for employment purposes and in accordance with legal requirements. Payroll records are retained for the period required by tax and employment law. Grievance records are retained according to employment dispute resolution timeframes.</p>

    <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Access your personal data held in the system</li>
        <li>Request corrections to inaccurate information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of data where no longer required</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint regarding privacy practices</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Compliance</h2>
    <p>This system complies with applicable New Zealand employment law and privacy principles. We take our privacy obligations seriously and handle all employee information with appropriate confidentiality.</p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy inquiries or concerns, please contact your system administrator or Human Resources department.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 30px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; font-size: 12px;">
        &copy; NZFTC EMS. All personal information is handled confidentially and securely.
    </p>
</div>
